From: AX6 EDMA correctness audit
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] edma_v1: fix TX teardown store index

edma_cleanup_txdesc_ring_res() uses txdesc->buffer_addr as the TX
store index to retrieve the skb, but buffer_addr is the DMA address
programmed into the TX descriptor, not the store index. The store
index is an opaque value returned by the firmware/hardware in the
completion descriptor or is maintained by the driver itself.

Use the ring position (descriptor index) as the store index, or
store the index in a separate driver-managed field. This prevents
out-of-bounds array access, wrong skb retrieval, and potential
crash on teardown.

Fixes F5 from AX6 cross-audit 2026-07-26.
⚠ PATCH NEEDS BUILD-TREE VERIFICATION: the teardown function name,
  descriptor structure, and store-index scheme must be confirmed
  against QSDK source. The correct fix may involve using the ring
  index directly or adding a dedicated store_idx field.

--- a/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v1/edma_cfg.c
+++ b/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v1/edma_cfg.c
@@ -XXX,XX +XXX,XX @@ static void edma_cleanup_txdesc_ring_res

 	for (i = 0; i < EDMA_TX_RING_SIZE; i++) {
 		txdesc = &edma_hw.txdesc_rings[ring].desc[i];
-		store_idx = txdesc->buffer_addr;
-		skb = tx_skb_store[store_idx];
+		/*
+		 * Use the ring index as store index — the store was
+		 * populated in ring order during TX. buffer_addr is
+		 * a DMA address, not a store index.
+		 */
+		skb = tx_skb_store[i];

 		if (!skb)
 			continue;

-		dma_unmap_single(dev, virt_to_phys(skb->data),
-				 skb_headlen(skb) + preheader,
+		dma_unmap_single(dev, tx_skb_store[i].dma_handle,
+				 tx_skb_store[i].dma_len,
 				 DMA_TO_DEVICE);
 		dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
+		tx_skb_store[i].skb = NULL;
+		tx_skb_store[i].dma_handle = 0;
 	}
